   349	Prop. 3.27 genuinely needs `D` nodal: in its proof the normalisation `H` must "intersect
   350	the closure of `q^{-1}(R) - H` transversally" in order to invoke Nori's Lemma 1.4, and at
   351	an `A_{2k-1}` the other branch meets `H` with multiplicity `k`. Two independent repairs
   352	follow; the second is complete.
   353	
   354	**5.1 Fallback (literature-only): blow up the tangential points.** Following Nori's own
   355	recipe (p. 307), blow up each `A_{2k_p-1}` point `k_p` times — each blow-up has
   356	multiplicity `2`, and after `k_p` of them the two branches are separated and meet the
   357	last exceptional curve transversally at distinct points, so the strict transform is
   358	smooth there. Put the exceptional curves into `E`; then `X'' - E = C^2 - {tangential
   359	points}` is still simply connected and `X'' - (D u E) = C^2 - D` is unchanged. The cost
   360	is `sum_j m_j^2 = 4 k_p` per tangential point, and `2r` now counts only the `s_1`
   361	remaining nodes. With `K_tac := sum_{p : k_p >= 2} k_p` and `delta_aff = s_1 + K_tac`,
   362	Nori's inequality `C'^2 - 4 K_tac > 2 s_1` becomes, on the coprime stratum,
   363	`nd - 4K_tac > (n-1)(d-1) - 2K_tac`, i.e.
   364	
   365	```text
   366	(B')     2 K_tac <= n + d - 2      ==>   pi_1(C^2 - D) abelian   ==>   NO.
   367	```
   368	
   369	`K_tac = 0` recovers Theorem B. `(B')` is unconditional and uses only the hashed Nori.
   370	
   371	**5.2 The complete repair: nodalization inside the parameter space.** Fix `gcd(n,d)=1`
   372	and let `P_{d,n} = {(p,q) : deg p = d, deg q = n}`, an irreducible quasi-affine variety
   373	(a Zariski-open subset of `C^{d+1} x C^{n+1}`). Every member is birational onto its image
   374	(a factorisation `gamma = gamma' o psi` with `deg psi = e` would force `e | gcd(d,n)=1`)
   375	and has one place at infinity at `Q = [1:0:0]`.
   376	
   377	**LEMMA 5.3 (`delta` is constant).** *On `P_{d,n}` with `gcd(n,d)=1`,
   378	`delta_infty = (d-n-1)(d-1)/2` and hence `delta_aff = (n-1)(d-1)/2` are constant.*
   379	*Proof.* The germ at `Q` is always parametrized by `(v,u) = (s^{d-n} beta, s^d alpha)`
   380	with `gcd(d-n,d)=1`, i.e. is always the `(d-n, d)`-cusp; then `(G)`. `[]`
   381	
   382	**LEMMA 5.4 (generic member is nodal).** *If `n >= 3` and `d >= 4`, the generic member of
   383	`P_{d,n}` is an immersion with only ordinary double points and no triple point.*
   384	*Proof.* Coefficient count: `{1,t,...,t^d}` and `{1,...,t^n}` separate `1`-jets at any
   385	two distinct parameters once `d, n >= 3`, so on `P_{d,n}` the conditions
   386	(i) `gamma'(t) = 0` (2 conditions on a 1-parameter family of `t`),
   387	(ii) `gamma(t_1) = gamma(t_2)` **and** the tangents agree (3 conditions on a 2-parameter
   388	family of pairs),
   389	(iii) `gamma(t_1) = gamma(t_2) = gamma(t_3)` (4 conditions on a 3-parameter family)
   390	are each independent, so each bad locus has codimension `>= 1` in `P_{d,n}`. `[]`
   391	
   392	(The hypothesis `n >= 3` is exactly what Theorem A(3) supplies once `phi` is assumed;
   393	`n <= 2` is already dead by Theorem A.)
   394	
   395	**LEMMA 5.5 (local shape of the degeneration).** *Let `D_0 in P_{d,n}` and let `D_t -> D_0`
   396	be nodal members. By 5.3 the total double-point length `delta_aff` is constant, so at
   397	each `p in Sing D_0` of type `A_{2k_p-1}` the length-`k_p` piece of the double-point
   398	scheme of `D_0` (supported at the single pair `(t_1^0, t_2^0)`) spreads into exactly
   399	`k_p` reduced pairs near `(t_1^0,t_2^0)`. Hence near `p`, `D_t` is two smooth branches —
   400	deformations of the two branches of `D_0` — crossing transversally at `k_p` points.*
   401	
   402	**LEMMA 5.6 (braid monodromy comparison).** *With the vertical projection of §1 fixed for
   403	both curves, and `t` small, choose disjoint discs `Y_i` in the `x`-line, one around each
   404	critical value of `D_0`, containing all critical values of `D_t` that converge to it.
   405	Then:*
   406	1. *over `partial Y_i` the two curves are isotopic, so the braid of `partial Y_i` is the
   407	   same factor `beta_i` for `D_0` and for `D_t`;*
   408	2. *for a disc around a vertical tangency or a node of `D_0` nothing splits, and the
   409	   relation is unchanged;*
